                        "form": "бурли́вей"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dfd7c548-97e7-3dcb-a948-23edb79d19d5",
                        "entry_id": "a282cd85-0b0a-3633-b57e-c67f8c183de6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "сильный, бурный (о воздушном или водном потоке, море); бурлящий, клокочущий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b23b7d5a-1bfa-4db6-8577-4aa3f7ad0984",
                                "sense_id": "dfd7c548-97e7-3dcb-a948-23edb79d19d5",
                                "text": "На сих полях имел сраженье с Карлом Петр / И шведов разметал, как прах бурливый ветр…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14981977-bfa9-4dc9-bb92-8b2556abd65b",
                                "sense_id": "dfd7c548-97e7-3dcb-a948-23edb79d19d5",
                                "text": "Кухарка бросилась к своему бурливому алтарю и застала на плите самый полный беспорядок: одно перекипело и било через край, другое перегорело, пережарилось и все наполняло смрадом помещение с потолка и до пола."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af234c34-7da7-3329-ac74-027b6fd6bc8a",
                        "entry_id": "a282cd85-0b0a-3633-b57e-c67f8c183de6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. разг. шумный, неспокойный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "98991ad5-5dca-4a7b-97e9-8c8ab41ed2ca",
                                "sense_id": "af234c34-7da7-3329-ac74-027b6fd6bc8a",
                                "text": "А нет, конечно, народа смирнее, покорнее и учтивее китайца, исключая кантонских: те, как и всякая чернь в больших городах, груба и бурлива."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d0da7279-857c-4b0d-965b-c09bd8226914",
                        "source_entry_id": "a282cd85-0b0a-3633-b57e-c67f8c183de6",
                        "target_lang_word": "seething",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "seething",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea680cf1-20de-3402-bb60-e26263bb8086",
                                        "entry_id": "a052db48-c0bd-301f-a3f2-d3c49a3dbcb3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Filled with unexpressed anger; in a state of being livid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb17daaf-acfd-3efb-b026-73ea902e2b52",
                                        "entry_id": "a052db48-c0bd-301f-a3f2-d3c49a3dbcb3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a state of extreme volatility; about to boil over; boiling, bubbling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ac884f6-d37e-4fa1-a5d5-376d043dfce5",
                                                "sense_id": "cb17daaf-acfd-3efb-b026-73ea902e2b52",
                                                "text": "There Grendel was watching his blood flow out into the seething tarn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9ebfa61-524f-4737-80c8-6fdf1ede8cfe",
                                                "sense_id": "cb17daaf-acfd-3efb-b026-73ea902e2b52",
                                                "text": "But as the nation’s most populous state stares down a seething climate crisis, one that cranked temperatures into triple digits last fall and set off a series of infernos that exploded, into bone dry air, the rebuilding process is beginning to look different."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e43a93d-153f-38a6-b635-8bb2ea82389a",
                                        "entry_id": "a052db48-c0bd-301f-a3f2-d3c49a3dbcb3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a state of unceasing and furious activity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "818fdd6f-1154-4f2e-b960-a4a6496dd070",
                                                "sense_id": "6e43a93d-153f-38a6-b635-8bb2ea82389a",
                                                "text": "Otis was unfeignedly thankful to lay down his work for a little while and escape from the seething, whining, weakly hive, impotent to help itself, but strong in its power to cripple, thwart, and annoy the sunken-eyed man, who, by official irony, was said to be “in charge” of it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "seething",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "895fa57a-51be-3495-b52a-eed155487e78",
                                        "entry_id": "eb9949c0-5a2a-3164-b8ec-85602ee8af11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The action of the verb to seethe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "831caf9d-448c-422b-adb4-903d705f241a",
                                                "sense_id": "895fa57a-51be-3495-b52a-eed155487e78",
                                                "text": "Over the winter-solid Roads, goes a great seething,— of mounted younger Gentlemen riding together by the dozens upon rented horses, Express Messengers in love with pure Velocity, Disgruntl'd Suitors with Pistols stuff'd in their Spatterdashes, seal'd Waggons not even a western Black-Boy would think of detaining."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "seething",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47355b21-808d-303b-bbce-0e2948b8a9c2",
                                        "entry_id": "5d26d76d-0036-338b-b8a6-649685ff6f4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of seethe"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d1809683-6d94-421b-a684-f66056b20b6c",
                        "source_entry_id": "a282cd85-0b0a-3633-b57e-c67f8c183de6",
                        "target_lang_word": "turbulent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "turbulent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6d5132c-3134-35b3-b70d-e8e6fb526d4b",
                                        "entry_id": "608ae88e-b480-31d4-b81d-8c534b3e8a61",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Violently disturbed or agitated; tempestuous, tumultuous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f820017-7318-4c0c-bc6d-9a27766c79bc",
                                                "sense_id": "c6d5132c-3134-35b3-b70d-e8e6fb526d4b",
                                                "text": "It is dangerous to sail in turbulent seas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3756a3b-ea6c-362a-a6d7-3299a54af57c",
                                        "entry_id": "608ae88e-b480-31d4-b81d-8c534b3e8a61",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Being in, or causing, disturbance or unrest."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea5c55ea-da20-41d3-95c8-ddd08db0dbd2",
                                                "sense_id": "f3756a3b-ea6c-362a-a6d7-3299a54af57c",
                                                "text": "The mid-19th century was a turbulent time in American history."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fceab3c-632e-4f39-a5ca-1308abb0f5df",
                                                "sense_id": "f3756a3b-ea6c-362a-a6d7-3299a54af57c",
                                                "text": "The [Washington] Post's proprietor through those turbulent [Watergate] days, Katharine Graham, held a double place in Washington’s hierarchy: at once regal Georgetown hostess and scrappy newshound, ready to hold the establishment to account. That is a very American position."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
